# API resources & envelope

One envelope for every `/api/*` response, produced centrally by `App\Support\ApiResponder` + the renderers in `bootstrap/app.php`:

```json
{ "status": "success|error", "message": "…", "data": { … } }
```

- Builders are `ApiResponder::success($data, $message, $code)` / `ApiResponder::error($message, $code, $data)`. Controllers return Resources, domain code throws — **never hand-assemble a different shape**.
- Validation failures (FormRequest) stay Laravel's `{message, errors}` 422 shape, **not** the envelope.
- CSRF mismatch returns `ApiResponder::error(..., 419)` as a response, not an `abort()`, so `HandleCors` can stamp `Access-Control-*`.
- `/batch` is read-only fan-in: outer 200 always, `meta: {failed, total}`, per-entry `{status, body}`. Callers inspect per-entry status.
- Error mapping table: [docs/platform/api-envelope.md](../../docs/platform/api-envelope.md).

## List contract (query mode only)

Index lists speak **one** mode. `display_mode` is optional and, when present, must be `query`; `display_mode=datatable` is **422** — validate through `App\Http\Requests\Concerns\InteractsWithListDisplayMode` (`listDisplayModeRules()`), never by hand.

- No paging params → `data` is a flat `T[]`. With `page` / `per_page` / `search` → `data: {items, pagination}` (`{current_page, last_page, per_page, total, has_more}`, default `per_page` 10, max 100).
- Query-mode rows carry **`actions[]`** built by a `QueryRowAction` builder — `App\Support\ListActions\Builders\` for a host domain, `App\Domain\{Domain}\Support\ListActions\` inside a package — attached with `QueryRowActionAttacher`. The SPA maps and executes them; **views must not invent keys**, and a key is a suggestion to the client, never a grant — every mutate path re-checks authorization server-side.
- Contract + lookups: [docs/platform/list-display-modes.md](../../docs/platform/list-display-modes.md).

## Aggregation (standalone-first)

`/batch` is a transport-level fan-in **for the SPA only** — never a replacement for a standalone endpoint.

- Every resource keeps its own directly-callable endpoint; the standalone route stays the source of truth. No endpoint may exist *only* inside an aggregated result.
- Aggregate a read **only when every sub-request would pass its own gates unchanged** (middleware, throttle, RBAC). Never bend a gate to make a read fit the batch — guest reads stay unbatched, mutations stay one-request-per-action.
- `/batch` re-dispatches through the full HTTP kernel, so a sub-request that would be rejected standalone is rejected inside the batch too (per-entry status; the caller falls back to its standalone loader).
- Policy: [docs/platform/api-aggregation.md](../../docs/platform/api-aggregation.md).

## Response data minimization (mandatory)

A JSON Resource is a **per-viewer contract**, not a model dump.

- Gate sensitive keys with `$this->when($request->user()?->can(...))` **or** split into a dedicated Resource. Never "hide it in the SPA" while the JSON still carries it.
- Guest/unauthenticated endpoints must not reuse owner Resources.
- Never emit: credential secrets or envelope plaintext; live accept/claim **tokens** to anyone but the token owner; upstream provider cost/rates to customers; FX/settlement internals to buyers; other users' emails to non-staff; storage `path`/`disk`/`checksum`/`region` to non-owner/non-staff.
- Every new list/show endpoint ships one **wrong-viewer 403** test and one **sensitive-field-absent** test (`Tests\Concerns\AssertsPayloadHygiene`).
- Full rules: [docs/platform/reference-security.md](../../docs/platform/reference-security.md#response-data-minimization-mandatory).
